  {
   "id": "do-now",
   "label": "Do Now: Read the Trace (1 of 2)",
   "type": "multiple-choice",
   "containerId": "y6-34-do-now",
   "content": "<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Do Now: Read the Trace (1 of 2)</h2><details class=\"lesson-tps\"><summary><span class=\"lesson-tps-steps\">Think <b>&rarr;</b> Pair <b>&rarr;</b> Share</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-q\">Why does each hop in a trace show an address, and not only a name?</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-reveal\">Show the answer</span></summary><div class=\"lesson-tps-a\"><p>Data finds each device by its address, so the address shows exactly which device the data went through.</p></div></details><p class=\"lesson-lead\">Recap of 6.3.3. Read the trace.</p><div class=\"igame-two-col\"><div><div style=\"font-family:var(--font-mono, monospace);font-size:17px;background:var(--surface-2);border:1px solid var(--line, var(--muted));border-radius:10px;padding:10px 14px;max-width:420px;margin:0 auto\"><div style=\"font-weight:700;margin-bottom:6px\">Trace route to www.music.example</div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:10px\"><span style=\"width:22px\">1.</span><span style=\"flex:1\">Home router</span><span style=\"color:var(--brand);font-weight:700\">192.168.1.1</span></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:10px\"><span style=\"width:22px\">2.</span><span style=\"flex:1\">Router A</span><span style=\"color:var(--brand);font-weight:700\">81.2.3.1</span></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:10px\"><span style=\"width:22px\">3.</span><span style=\"flex:1\">Router E</span><span style=\"color:var(--brand);font-weight:700\">81.2.3.5</span></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:10px\"><span style=\"width:22px\">4.</span><span style=\"flex:1\">Web server</span><span style=\"color:var(--brand);font-weight:700\">198.51.100.20</span></div></div></div><div id=\"y6-34-do-now\"></div></div>",
   "items": [
    {
     "prompt": "What is the address of the web server that keeps www.music.example?",
     "options": [
      "81.2.3.5",
      "192.168.1.1",
      "198.51.100.20"
     ],
     "correct": 2,
     "explain": "The last hop is the web server: 198.51.100.20. The other hops are routers."
    },
    {
     "prompt": "How many routers are on the way to the web server?",
     "options": [
      "4",
      "3",
      "2"
     ],
     "correct": 1,
     "explain": "Home router, Router A, Router E: 3 routers. Hop 4 is the web server."
    }
   ],
   "walkthrough": {
    "title": "Walk me through it: reading a trace",
    "steps": [
     {
      "text": "<strong>A similar trace.</strong> 1. Home router 192.168.0.1, 2. Router K 62.1.1.1, 3. Web server 203.0.113.50.",
      "visual": "<div class=\"wt-note\">3 hops</div>"
     },
     {
      "text": "Which hop keeps the website? Look at the <strong>last</strong> hop.",
      "visual": "<p style=\"margin:10px 0 0;text-align:center;font-size:20px;font-family:var(--font-mono, monospace)\">3. Web server <span class=\"wt-hl\">203.0.113.50</span></p>"
     },
     {
      "text": "Now count the routers. Skip the last hop: it is not a router.",
      "visual": "<p style=\"margin:10px 0 0;text-align:center;font-size:20px;font-family:var(--font-mono, monospace)\"><span class=\"wt-hl\">Home router</span>, <span class=\"wt-hl\">Router K</span></p>"
     },
     {
      "text": "Here that is 2 routers. Now read the Do Now trace in the same way: last hop first, then count the routers before it.",
      "visual": "<div class=\"wt-note\">last hop, then count the routers</div>"
     }
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "do-now-2",
   "label": "Do Now: Addresses (2 of 2)",
   "type": "short-answer-validation",
   "validatorId": "y6-34-do-now-2",
   "validatorKey": "y6_34_do_now_2",
   "content": "<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Do Now: Addresses (2 of 2)</h2><details class=\"lesson-tps\"><summary><span class=\"lesson-tps-steps\">Think <b>&rarr;</b> Pair <b>&rarr;</b> Share</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-q\">Why does data need to carry an address at all?</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-reveal\">Show the answer</span></summary><div class=\"lesson-tps-a\"><p>So the switches and routers know which device it is for, and send it the right way.</p></div></details><p class=\"lesson-lead\">Recap of 6.3.3. Type your answers.</p><div class=\"lesson-exam-card\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-responses\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y6-34-do-now-2-a\">Ben and Chi both have the address 10.0.0.4. Ana has 10.0.0.6. Type a new address for Chi. Keep 10.0.0. at the start.</label><input id=\"y6-34-do-now-2-a\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"do-now-2-a\" aria-label=\"Do Now: Addresses (2 of 2) part a\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y6-34-do-now-2-b\">You open www.music.example. What kind of computer sends you its pages? Type two words.</label><input id=\"y6-34-do-now-2-b\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"do-now-2-b\" aria-label=\"Do Now: Addresses (2 of 2) part b\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-actions\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y6-34-do-now-2-check\">Check answers</button><strong>Total: 2 marks</strong></div><div id=\"y6-34-do-now-2-feedback\" class=\"pseudocode-feedback\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"></div></div>",
   "walkthrough": {
    "title": "Walk me through it: a free address",
    "steps": [
     {
      "text": "<strong>A similar question.</strong> Mai and Tom both have 172.16.0.8. Lee has 172.16.0.5. Give Tom a new address.",
