  {
   "id": "help-desk",
   "label": "Network Help Desk: Search Calls",
   "content": "<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Network Help Desk: Search Calls</h2><details class=\"lesson-tps\"><summary><span class=\"lesson-tps-steps\">Think <b>&rarr;</b> Pair <b>&rarr;</b> Share</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-q\">Why tell the customer better search terms, and not only the answer?</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-reveal\">Show the answer</span></summary><div class=\"lesson-tps-a\"><p>Next time they can find it on their own.</p></div></details><p class=\"lesson-lead\"><strong>About 15 minutes.</strong> Customers phone you. They cannot find something on the web. Use today's lesson to help them.</p><ol class=\"lesson-facts\" style=\"font-size:20px;line-height:1.5\"><li><strong>Open a new tab.</strong> Type the class game address your teacher shows on the board. Type your name.</li><li><strong>Take the two training calls first.</strong> Do what the arrow shows.</li><li><strong>Read the customer's search.</strong> What is wrong with it: too few words, a spelling mistake, or a word with two meanings?</li><li><strong>Search on the desk computer</strong> with clear search terms. Open the page that answers the customer.</li><li><strong>Tell the customer</strong> the answer and the better search terms, then explain why their search did not work.</li><li>Calling the Tech Lead for help costs points. Try first, then ask.</li></ol>"
  },
  {
   "id": "plenary",
   "label": "Plenary: Searching the Web Drill",
   "type": "embedded-app",
   "appId": "drill-y6-3-4-isearch",
   "embedContainerId": "y6-34-plenary",
   "content": "<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Plenary: Searching the Web Drill</h2><details class=\"lesson-tps\"><summary><span class=\"lesson-tps-steps\">Think <b>&rarr;</b> Pair <b>&rarr;</b> Share</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-q\">Why does the drill bring back a question you got wrong?</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-reveal\">Show the answer</span></summary><div class=\"lesson-tps-a\"><p>Getting it right again later shows you remember it, not that you guessed once.</p></div></details><p class=\"lesson-lead\"><strong>About 4 minutes.</strong> Search engines, ranking and clear search terms. Your progress is saved.</p><div id=\"y6-34-plenary\"></div>"
  }
 ],
